IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fta-types`
IMPORT `fta-transactions`

-- Fair Trading Act 1986 — GOAL 3: CONSUMER INFORMATION AND SAFETY.
--
--   "Does a standard bind goods marked for export; how long does an unsafe
--    goods notice last; by when must a voluntary recall be notified; and how
--    long may a suspension of supply notice last?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_121.txt — Parts 2-4,
-- ss 27-36.

§ `Goal 3 — consumer information and safety`

-- ss 28(3), 30(3): a consumer information or product safety standard does
-- not apply "to goods that are intended for use outside New Zealand if there
-- is applied to the goods— (a) a statement that the goods are for export
-- only; or (b) a statement indicating ... that the goods are intended to be
-- used outside New Zealand".
@ref ss 28, 30
GIVEN `standard exists` IS A BOOLEAN, complied IS A BOOLEAN, `marked for export` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `supplying the goods breaches the standard, a standard applies:` `standard exists` `, complied:` complied `, marked for export:` `marked for export` IF
    `standard exists` AND (NOT complied) AND (NOT `marked for export`)

-- s 31(2) "A notice made pursuant to subsection (1) shall, unless previously
-- revoked ..., remain in force for 18 months after the date of publication".
-- Only a s 31(1) notice: a s 31(1A) notice (reasonably foreseeable misuse)
-- has no statutory expiry (noted after the independent pass).
-- (3) after 18 months, with no product safety standard, the Minister may
-- prohibit supply.
@ref s 31(2)-(3)
GIVEN published IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day an unsafe goods notice is in force, published` published MEANS
    `add months` published 18

-- s 31A(2) "The supplier must, within 2 working days after recalling the
-- goods, notify the chief executive of the recall."
@ref s 31A(2)
GIVEN recalled IS A DATE, cal IS A `Working day calendar`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify a voluntary recall, recalled` recalled `, calendar` cal MEANS
    `the` 2 `th working day after` recalled `, calendar` cal

-- s 33D(3)(b) a suspension of supply notice expires "no later than 5 pm on the
-- third working day after the day on which the notice is issued"; (5) it may
-- be renewed "not more than twice" and not "so that the total prohibition
-- exceeds 9 consecutive working days".
@ref s 33D(3), (5)
GIVEN issued IS A DATE, cal IS A `Working day calendar`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day a suspension of supply notice may run to, issued` issued `, calendar` cal MEANS
    `the` 3 `th working day after` issued `, calendar` cal

@ref s 33D(5)
GIVEN renewals IS A NUMBER, `working days in total` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the renewals are within s 33D(5), renewals` renewals `, working days in total` `working days in total` IF
    renewals AT MOST 2 AND `working days in total` AT MOST 9
